OL,3,ATrans people should use hospital spaces
OL,4,Aaccording to biological sex, NHS
OL,5,AEngland says
OL,6,
OL,7,FTrans patients should be cared for on
OL,8,Fsingle-sex hospital wards or bays that
OL,9,Falign with their biological sex rather
OL,10,Fthan their gender identity, according
OL,11,Fto new NHS England (NHSE) guidance.
OL,13,FIt says when this is not "clinically
OL,14,Fappropriate" then alternative
OL,15,Farrangements should be made.
OL,17,FBut the guidance also says decisions
OL,18,Fmay have to be made on a case-by-case
OL,19,Fbasis and must ensure clinical needs
OL,20,Fare met, and that the dignity and
OL,21,Fsafety of the trans patient and of
OL,22,Fother patients are maintained.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/39
